# `results/` — Generated outputs (DO NOT EDIT)

Everything here is a **build target**: produced by the pipeline, regenerable, and
gitignored. Figures (`figures/light/`, `figures/dark/`) and tables (`tables/`).

**Never edit anything in this folder by hand.** Your changes will be silently
overwritten the next time the pipeline runs. To change a result, edit the code in
`src/` or a parameter in `conf/` and rerun:

```bash
snakemake results/figures/light/fig3.pdf   # rebuild one target
snakemake                                  # rebuild everything
```

## Figures: light vs dark
- `figures/light/` — canonical, for print and papers (dark-on-white).
- `figures/dark/` — derived, for on-screen slides (light-on-transparent).

Both come from the same plotting code and the palette in `conf/theme/`. See the
theme system in [`../conf/theme/`](../conf/theme/).

## This is for *generated* figures only
Hand-drawn schematics and diagrams are **inputs**, not outputs — they live in
[`../assets/figures/`](../assets/figures/) and are git-tracked.
